      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No data returned for that event/date — schedule seems stale or empty in this session. I won't guess at its contents.\n\n**Bottom line:** No strict overhead press, 3x/week or otherwise, until the surgeon clears overhead loading (restriction runs to roughly week 12 post-op — you're at ~week 4 now per your profile). This isn't a volume/intensity knob I can turn down; it's a hard medical constraint.\n\nWhat I'll program instead on Wednesday and through the week, keeping the pressing pattern \"warm\" without loading the joint overhead:\n- **Scapular control:** Face Pulls, Face Pulls with External Rotation, Prone YTWs, Band Pull-Aparts\n- **Rotator cuff:** Band External Rotation, Posterior Rotator Cuff Stretch\n- **Non-overhead pressing/pulling to keep upper-body strength:** Landmine Press + Reach (low-angle, not overhead), Chest-Supported Dumbbell Row, Seated Cable Row, Lat Pulldown\n\nSay the word and I'll build out Wednesday's session with this list now. When you get surgeon clearance (or a revised timeline), tell me and I'll stand up the overhead progression immediately — light dumbbell presses first, strict barbell later."
